      "text": "Monteverde – Manuel Antonio National Park"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "86974520bc54f2659c373a94b415ba4b41d6b72518b743621db75315b237fa5b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6lyzli-ohxi6gztz2",
        "model": "ChatGPT Codex"
      },
      "text": "Travel to the Manuel Antonio area.\n\nThe afternoon is free.\n\nManuel Antonio National Park combines rainforest, white-sand beaches, coral reefs and a stretch of Pacific coastline.\n\nAlong the forest trails, you may spot sloths, monkeys, toucans and other wildlife. You can relax and swim at the beaches or snorkel in the coastal waters.\n\nFollow the park rules during your visit and take care around local plants and wildlife.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast."
    },
